From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:17:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PM / devfreq: mtk-cci: set the rate of the OPP it picked

The target callback looks up the OPP for the requested rate, takes its
voltage, and then sets the clock to the requested rate rather than to
the OPP's rate. It also ignores the devfreq flags and always takes the
highest OPP at or below the request.

That holds only while every requested rate is an OPP, as it is when the
passive governor follows the CPU through required-opps. Without
required-opps the passive governor interpolates between the CPU and
CCI tables, and the request falls between two OPPs. The CCI then runs
above the rate its voltage was chosen for. On an MT6797 a request of
626.08 MHz between the 611 and 676 MHz OPPs ran the CCI at 625 MHz on
the 611 MHz voltage. devfreq also could not find that rate in its table
for the transition statistics.

Pass the devfreq flags to devfreq_recommended_opp() and let it round
the rate to the OPP it returns, as the other devfreq drivers do. Without
the least-upper-bound flag that is the lowest OPP at or above the
request, so the voltage and the clock come from the same OPP, and
devfreq records the rate that was set.
---
 drivers/devfreq/mtk-cci-devfreq.c | 21 ++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/mtk-cci-devfreq.c b/drivers/devfreq/mtk-cci-devfreq.c
index 4a780028b..b5a6b34a5 100644
--- a/drivers/devfreq/mtk-cci-devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/mtk-cci-devfreq.c
@@ -134,24 +134,23 @@ static int mtk_ccifreq_target(struct device *dev, unsigned long *freq,
 	if (!drv)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (drv->pre_freq == *freq)
-		return 0;
-
-	mutex_lock(&drv->reg_lock);
-
-	inter_voltage = drv->inter_voltage;
-
 	opp_rate = *freq;
-	opp = devfreq_recommended_opp(dev, &opp_rate, 1);
+	opp = devfreq_recommended_opp(dev, freq, flags);
 	if (IS_ERR(opp)) {
-		dev_err(dev, "failed to find opp for freq: %ld\n", opp_rate);
-		ret = PTR_ERR(opp);
-		goto out_unlock;
+		dev_err(dev, "failed to find opp for freq: %lu\n", opp_rate);
+		return PTR_ERR(opp);
 	}
 
 	voltage = dev_pm_opp_get_voltage(opp);
 	dev_pm_opp_put(opp);
 
+	if (drv->pre_freq == *freq)
+		return 0;
+
+	mutex_lock(&drv->reg_lock);
+
+	inter_voltage = drv->inter_voltage;
+
 	pre_voltage = regulator_get_voltage(drv->proc_reg);
 	if (pre_voltage < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "invalid vproc value: %d\n", pre_voltage);
-- 
